# Database drivers for the Python worker, beside requirements-gis.txt. Each
# is needed only for its own connection type; the worker reports a clear
# error for a connection whose driver is missing.
#
# - psycopg: PostgreSQL / PostGIS (postgis).
# - oracledb: Oracle (oracle, sde-oracle), in thin mode: pure Python, no
#   Oracle Instant Client.
# - pyodbc: SQL Server (sqlserver, mssql, sde-sqlserver, azure-sql). Also
#   needs Microsoft ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server installed on the machine
#   (Windows: the msodbcsql18 installer; Linux: the msodbcsql18 package).
#
# This is the source: requirements-db.txt is generated from it (exact
# versions and SHA-256 hashes, resolved together with requirements-gis.txt
# so the two install side by side). Edit this file, then run
#   python packaging/engine/compile-requirements.py
psycopg[binary]>=3.2,<4
oracledb>=2.0
pyodbc>=5.1,<6
